# Fixtures are inputs, never build outputs. Opening one of these trees with a
# real jdtls or running gradle in it leaves .gradle/, .project and .settings/
# behind — and a committed .project is not inert: jdtls treats the tree as an
# already-imported Eclipse project, so a spec's behaviour would depend on
# whatever an earlier debugging session happened to leave here.
.gradle/
.settings/
.project
.classpath
build/
bin/
